{"id":2813,"path":"/grammar-points/a2/subject-questions-questions-preposition/","parentId":542,"order":10,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a2","depth":3,"title":"Subject questions, questions with preposition","seo":{"title":"Subject questions, questions with preposition - Test-English","description":"Learn how to form subject questions and preposition questions in this A2 grammar lesson. Clear rules, charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/A2%E2%80%93Subject-questions_Questions-with-preposition.png"},"modified":"2026-02-19T10:44:16","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct options to complete the questions about the underlined words. Some of the questions are subject questions and questions with preposition.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"342\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct&nbsp;forms to complete the questions about the underlined words. Some of the questions are subject questions and questions with preposition.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"343\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Write&nbsp;questions for the underlined words. Some of the questions are subject questions and questions with preposition.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"344\"></div>"],"explanation":"<h2>Subject questions and object questions</h2> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-29267\" src=\"/media/uploads/Subject-questions-grammar-chart.webp\" alt=\"Grammar diagram illustrating the structure of subject questions in English, contrasting correct and incorrect usage with examples.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <p>In the <strong>present and past simple</strong> tenses, we do not use an auxiliary verb (<strong>do/does</strong> or <strong>did</strong>) after the question word if the question word (<strong>who, what, etc.</strong>) is the subject of the sentence.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Who did win</strong></span> the match? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Who won</strong></span> the match? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>What did happen</strong></span> last night? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>What happened</strong></span>&nbsp;last night?</em> <em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>How many people did go</strong></span> to the party? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><span><strong>How many people went</strong></span> to the party? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <p>This rule applies specifically to the <strong>present and past simple</strong> tenses. For other tenses (present continuous, present perfect, etc), where the <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/auxiliary-verbs-do-be-and-have/\">auxiliary verb</a> is part of the verb form, we include the auxiliary verbs in subject questions.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Who <span><strong>is</strong></span>&nbsp;cooking dinner tonight?</em></li> <li><em>Who <span><strong>has</strong></span> eaten all the cookies?</em></li> </ul> <p>When we are asking about the object (after the verb), we use the normal order of the <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/questions/\">English question</a>: <strong>auxiliary verb + subject</strong>. These types of questions are called object questions.</p> <h4>Object question vs subject question</h4> <div class=\"infoblock\"> <div class=\"tg-wrap\"> <table class=\"tg\"> <tbody> <tr> <td class=\"tg-031e\"> <p>Jack called <span class=\"highlighter\">Teresa</span>. (Teresa = object)</p> </td> <td class=\"tg-031e\"> <p><span class=\"highlighter\">Jack</span> called Teresa. (Jack = subject)</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td class=\"tg-031e\"> <p><span class=\"highlighter\">Who</span> did Jack call? (Who = object)</p> </td> <td class=\"tg-031e\"> <p><span class=\"highlighter\">Who</span> called Teresa? (Who = subject)</p> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> </div> <h2>Questions with preposition</h2> <p>In informal or spoken English, when a question word needs a preposition, the preposition goes at the end of the question (after the verb or after verb + object if there is an object). We don’t use the preposition at the beginning.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I played tennis <span><strong>with John</strong></span>. </em>⇒<em>&nbsp;<span><strong>Who</strong></span> did you play tennis <span><strong>with</strong></span>?&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I work <span><strong>for a multinational company </strong></span></em>⇒<em>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span><strong>What</strong></span> company do you work <span><strong>for</strong></span>?</em></li> <li><em>We usually talk <span><strong>about sports</strong></span>. </em>⇒ <em><span><strong>What</strong></span> do you usually talk <span><strong>about</strong></span>?&nbsp;</em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":342,"questions":[{"id":2927,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She is looking <span>for a job</span>.&nbsp;⇒ What <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["is she looking","is she looking for","she's looking for"]}]},{"id":2928,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span>Sonya</span> helped me with the boxes.&nbsp;⇒ Who <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> with the boxes?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["helped you","did you help","did help you"]}]},{"id":2929,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I asked&nbsp;<span>John</span> to bring music for the party.&nbsp;⇒ Who <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to bring music for the party?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["asked you","you asked","did you ask"]}]},{"id":2930,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I am waiting <span>for my husband</span>.&nbsp;⇒ Who <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["are you waiting for","you're waiting for","are you waiting"]}]},{"id":2931,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span>Very few people</span> went to the party.&nbsp;⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to the party?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["How many did people go","How many people went","How many people did go"]}]},{"id":2932,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She invited <span>very few people</span> to the party&nbsp;⇒ How many people <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to the party?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["invited she","did she invite","she invited"]}]},{"id":2933,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He apologised <span>for being late</span>.&nbsp;⇒ What <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["he did apologise for","did he apologise","did he apologise for"]}]},{"id":2934,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Sam loves <span>Elisa</span>.&nbsp;⇒ Who <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["does Sam love","loves Sam","Sam loves"]}]},{"id":2935,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span>Something terrible</span> happened last night.&nbsp;⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> last night?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["What did happen","Who happened","What happened"]}]},{"id":2936,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The book is based <span>on a novel by a Russian writer</span>.&nbsp;⇒ What <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["the book is based","is the book based","is the book based on"]}]}]},{"id":343,"questions":[{"id":2947,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I dreamt <span>about our old house in Cornwall</span>.&nbsp;⇒ What _____?</div>","choices":[{"id":5063,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>dreamt you</span>"},{"id":5064,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>dreamt you about</span>"},{"id":5065,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>did you dream about</span>"}]},{"id":2948,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I always listen <span>to Jack's advice</span>.&nbsp;⇒ What _____?</div>","choices":[{"id":5066,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>you do always listen to</span>"},{"id":5067,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>do you always listen to</span>"},{"id":5068,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>do you always listen</span>"}]},{"id":2949,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div><span>Jason</span> kissed Virginia at the playground. ⇒&nbsp;_____ at the playground?</div>","choices":[{"id":5069,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Who kissed Virginia</span>"},{"id":5070,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Who did kiss Virginia</span>"},{"id":5071,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Who did Virginia kiss</span>"}]},{"id":2950,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Jason kissed <span>Virginia</span> at the playground. ⇒&nbsp;_____ at the playground?</div>","choices":[{"id":5072,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Who Jason kissed </span>"},{"id":5073,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Who did Jason kiss</span>"},{"id":5074,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Who kissed Jason</span>"}]},{"id":2951,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Lewis&nbsp;asked his boss <span>for a promotion</span>.&nbsp;⇒ What _____?</div>","choices":[{"id":5075,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Lewis did ask his boss for</span>"},{"id":5076,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Lewis asked his boss for</span>"},{"id":5077,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>did Lewis ask his boss for</span>"}]},{"id":2952,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div><span>Lewis</span>&nbsp;asked his boss for a promotion.&nbsp;⇒ _____ for a promotion?</div>","choices":[{"id":5078,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Who asked his boss</span>"},{"id":5079,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Who did he ask his boss</span>"},{"id":5080,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Who did ask his boss</span>"}]},{"id":2953,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Lewis&nbsp;asked <span>his boss</span> for a promotion.&nbsp;⇒ _____ for a promotion?</div>","choices":[{"id":5081,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Who did Lewis ask</span>"},{"id":5082,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Who asked Lewis</span>"},{"id":5083,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Who did ask Lewis</span>"}]},{"id":2954,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I'm happy <span>about the results</span>.&nbsp;⇒ What _____?</div>","choices":[{"id":5084,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>are you happy</span>"},{"id":5085,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>are you happy about</span>"},{"id":5086,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>you're happy about</span>"}]},{"id":2955,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Alexander Graham Bell invented <span>the telephone</span>.&nbsp;⇒ What _____?</div>","choices":[{"id":5087,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>did Alexander Graham Bell invent</span>"},{"id":5088,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>invented Alexander Graham Bell</span>"},{"id":5089,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>did invent Alexander Graham Bell</span>"}]},{"id":2956,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div><span>Alexander Fleming</span> discovered penicillin.&nbsp;⇒ Who _____?</div>","choices":[{"id":5090,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>did Alexander Fleming discover</span>"},{"id":5091,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>did discover penicillin</span>"},{"id":5092,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>discovered penicillin </span>"}]}]},{"id":344,"questions":[{"id":2937,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I came to see <u>you</u>.&nbsp;⇒ Who <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2938,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She is worried&nbsp;<span>about you</span>.&nbsp;⇒ Who <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2939,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I travelled to India <span>with my boyfriend</span>.&nbsp;⇒ Who <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2940,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><u>George</u>&nbsp;arrives late every day. ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> every day?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2941,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He was looking <span>at the new building</span>. ⇒ What <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2942,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He is writing <span>from Paris</span>.&nbsp;⇒ Where <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2943,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I informed&nbsp;<span>John</span> about the meeting.&nbsp;⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> about the meeting?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2945,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span>My manager</span> informed John about the meeting.&nbsp;⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> about the meeting?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2944,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span>A car&nbsp;accident</span> caused him multiple fractures. ⇒ What <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> multiple fractures?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":2946,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She believes<span> in ghosts</span>.&nbsp;⇒ What <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}